    <div data-figma-id="275:112" class="d-fec54b112">
      <p data-figma-id="275:113" class="d-2e58b8325">
        WHAT I ACTUALLY LEARNED
      </p>
      <p data-figma-id="275:114" class="d-bdb11de03">
        Internal tools don't need convincing, they need getting out of the way. I spent two days
        designing for a visitor who was never coming.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p data-figma-id="275:115" class="d-f6aa38a40">
      <span class="d-47084631e">
        The dashboard underneath it was closer to right. It already had the two ideas that survived
        all the way to the end: a{' '}
      </span>
      <span class="d-6df3d0592">category tag</span>
      <span class="d-47084631e"> (Software, Hardware, Data) and an </span>
      <span class="d-6df3d0592">impact level</span>
      <span class="d-47084631e">
        {' '}
        on every update — and a &quot;Why it matters&quot; line explaining the news instead of just
        reporting it.
      </span>
    </p>
